#: skills/workflows/getting-started.bpmn:86
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Derives the URL and holds the three-way report that follows it: \"live\", \"not-yet\" and \"unknown\" are reached by exclusive branches of one DMN-computed gateway, and this lane is what keeps a failed probe from being reported as the softer \"not-yet\" it would be tempting to default to."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/getting-started.bpmn:100
#. Diagram label
msgid "Detect the interaction modality"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/getting-started.bpmn:72
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every write in this diagram belongs to this lane, and each sits behind the non-relaxable read-first gate: nothing is created or scaffolded until Gateway_Intent has classified what was actually asked for, which is what stands between this lane and writing over somebody's existing project."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/getting-started.bpmn:52
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "folio-assistant — getting started: from \"create a folio\" to a live site. \"Create a folio\" is five different requests. Gateway_Intent computes which one from decisions/folio-intent.dmn rather than letting the agent assume, and `ask` is one of the outcomes the table can return. Gateway_Live applies the same construction to publication, with `unknown` kept distinct from `not-yet`. Source of truth: this file. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it by `bun run render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG."
msgstr ""

